=== PROMPT-SET COLLISION + RESOLUTION (Covenant rule 9 — no silent drift) ===
================================================================================
Two distinct prompts in this tier are BOTH titled "ConfirmDialog" and BOTH declare the SAME native
output glob `apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/ConfirmDialog.*`:
  • P-0001 (THIS prompt)  -> web source components/ai/ConfirmDialog.tsx  -> export `AiConfirmDialog`
        (AI tool-use approval: title "Approve Helix action", intro, Tool name, JSON Arguments,
         Approve / Cancel; i18n keys ai.confirm.title/intro.mutates/intro.read/toolLabel/argsLabel/
         run/cancel).
  • P-0012 (already shipped, committed f5a7add1a) -> web source components/ui/ConfirmDialog.tsx ->
        export `ConfirmDialog` (destructive dialog: severity, typed-confirmation gate, silence
        opt-out; keys confirm.*).
The committed `ConfirmDialog.*` files are the 0012 DESTRUCTIVE port; they do NOT implement the AI
dialog spec (no "Approve Helix action" / "Tool" / "Arguments" / ai.confirm.* keys). Declaring 0001
"done" against them would be red-as-green.

Resolution (faithful + non-destructive): the two web components have DIFFERENT export names, so the
AI surface ships as native `AiConfirmDialog` in NEW files within the allowed `ConfirmDialog.*` glob
(`ConfirmDialog.Ai.swift`, `.AiAdapter`, `.AiSeams`, `.AiModel`, `.AiStates`, `.AiViews`,
`.AiPreviews`, `.AiTests`, `.AiModelTests`, `.Ai.strings`), with a distinct, collision-free
`AiConfirm*` type prefix — ALONGSIDE the 0012 `Confirm*`/`ConfirmDialog*` types. Both surfaces
coexist (native mirrors the web 1:1: `AiConfirmDialog` ⇄ `AiConfirmDialog`, `ConfirmDialog` ⇄
`ConfirmDialog`). 0012 is preserved; no shared file touched. `grep -c "AiConfirm" before` = 0 across
the module (verified unique before writing).

================================================================================
=== WEB-PARITY MAP (components/ai/ConfirmDialog.tsx -> native) ===
================================================================================
  props open / tool {name, description?, mutates} / args / onConfirm / onCancel / loading
                                              -> AiConfirmRequest (tool + arguments + loading)
                                                 pushed by AiConfirmDialogSource; the two decisions
                                                 behind AiConfirmDialogController seam.
  t('ai.confirm.title','Approve Helix action')        -> AiConfirmDialogProjection.title
  tool.mutates ? intro.mutates : intro.read           -> AiConfirmDialogProjection.intro
  t('ai.confirm.toolLabel','Tool') + tool.name (mono) -> AiConfirmDialogToolSection (monospaced name)
  tool.description (optional)                          -> AiConfirmDialogToolSection description
  t('ai.confirm.argsLabel','Arguments')               -> AiConfirmDialogArgumentsSection label
  JSON.stringify(args ?? {}, null, 2)                 -> AiConfirmDialogProjection.prettyPrintedArguments
        (2-space indent; `{}` when empty — matches the web "renders empty {} when args is null" test)
  t('ai.confirm.run','Approve') / t('ai.confirm.cancel','Cancel') -> confirmLabel / cancelLabel
  Button loading -> spinner + disabled                -> AiConfirmDialogActions (TSButton isLoading)
  Modal onClose = loading ? noop : onCancel           -> model.dismiss() (swallowed while busy)
  onConfirm (await continuation) / onCancel           -> model.confirm() (async, submitting) / cancel()
  open=false -> Modal renders null                    -> resolveVisibility -> .hidden (EmptyView)

  States reproduced (every one renders real chrome — engineering guideline #6, never a blank box):
    loading (request resolving) | empty (nothing to approve) | error (delivery failed + retry)
    | content (the approval form) | inline-error (cached request + failed reload)
    | freshness chip Live/Stale/Offline + cached-data banner (ADR-013)
    | in-flight submitting (web `loading`: buttons disabled + confirm spinner)
  Native affordance beyond the web (data-bound, not scope creep): a mutates/read-only chip + a
  field-count VoiceOver summary derived from the SAME `tool.mutates` / `args` data.

  Telemetry: `view.opened` with surface slug "ConfirmDialog" (per prompt) via AiConfirmDialogTelemetry
  (OSLog default; production injects the P1/S11 diagnostics sink).

